now a special early mother's day  celebration today the reunion of a mom  and baby who nearly lost their lives to  covet reuniting with the icu team of  doctors and nurses at southern hills  hospital who helped save their lives  an icu team that came together as a  family to help save rowena salas's life  and that of her premature baby oliver  there are moments in your career that  that like make you and they change you  for the better and that will be that day  forever for me thanksgiving day last  year rowena in a dire situation fighting  covet plummeting oxygen levels rushed to  southern hills hospital i know a lot of  us had  been like worried about this family as a  whole we prayed about it physicians  performing an emergency c-section on  baby oliver who was just seven months  old he recovered in the nicu rowena had  to be intubated fighting for her life in  the icu miracle  you know she's obviously invincible  rowena's husband wasn't as fortunate  losing his battle with covid six months  prior with the preemie rowena wasn't  prepared nurses and staff created a baby  registry delivering hundreds of items to  help the family it fills my heart when i  saw them and just when she was  introducing all of them the care that  they provided it makes me tear up right  now even just talking about it  but i'm just grateful for everybody and  everything  celebrating an early mother's day with  her two children and the staff she feels  beyond fortunate as you all know  mother's day last year wasn't so great  i lost my husband the day  after  it's just something i have to work with  and just process  but i am grateful to be here today to be  able to care for my babies
 

